  "summary": "A magnetic coupling transmits torque through a sealed wall without any shaft seal. Permanent magnets on an outer rotor (on the motor shaft) attract the opposite poles of magnets on an inner rotor (on the pump or mixer shaft). A thin, non-magnetic containment shell separates the two, so the process fluid is completely sealed — ideal for toxic, flammable or valuable liquids.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Coupling (non-contact)",
    "type": "Synchronous coaxial permanent-magnet coupling"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "magnets": "12 per rotor, alternating N/S",
    "shell": "Stainless (eddy-current losses) — non-metallic shells avoid losses"
  },
